<!-- FAQ -->
<section class="bg-canvas py-20 px-6 md:px-8">
  <div class="max-w-[640px] mx-auto">
    <h2 class="font-serif font-normal text-[2.25rem] leading-[1.15] mb-8 text-ink">Questions families ask</h2>

    <div class="divide-y divide-hair">

      <details class="group py-4">
        <summary class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4 cursor-pointer list-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
          <span class="text-ink text-[.9375rem] font-medium">We're just starting out, isn't this overkill?</span>
          {% icon "chevron-down", "w-4 h-4 text-muted shrink-0 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" %}
        </summary>
        <p class="text-dim text-[.9375rem] leading-relaxed opacity-80 mt-3">
          Not at all. The earlier you start, the less there is to untangle later. Add as little or as much as you like, there's no setup to finish before it's useful.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="group py-4">
        <summary class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4 cursor-pointer list-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
          <span class="text-ink text-[.9375rem] font-medium">Can we both use it, or just one of us?</span>
          {% icon "chevron-down", "w-4 h-4 text-muted shrink-0 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" %}
        </summary>
        <p class="text-dim text-[.9375rem] leading-relaxed opacity-80 mt-3">
          Either. Many couples set it up together on one device, or each keep their own and combine the picture during a conversation.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="group py-4">
        <summary class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4 cursor-pointer list-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
          <span class="text-ink text-[.9375rem] font-medium">Do we need a will already?</span>
          {% icon "chevron-down", "w-4 h-4 text-muted shrink-0 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" %}
        </summary>
        <p class="text-dim text-[.9375rem] leading-relaxed opacity-80 mt-3">
          No. Collator helps you record what exists today. If you don't have a will yet, having everything organised makes it much easier to see what one would need to cover, when you're ready.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="group py-4">
        <summary class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4 cursor-pointer list-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
          <span class="text-ink text-[.9375rem] font-medium">Is any of this shared with you, or with anyone else?</span>
          {% icon "chevron-down", "w-4 h-4 text-muted shrink-0 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" %}
        </summary>
        <p class="text-dim text-[.9375rem] leading-relaxed opacity-80 mt-3">
          No. Everything stays on the device it's entered on, and in your own backup if you enable one. Read more on our <a href="/privacy" class="text-saffron hover:text-saffron-deep transition-colors">privacy page</a>.
        </p>
      </details>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

